<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
   Auto Backup policy for Android 11 and older (API 31+ uses
   data_extraction_rules.xml instead).

   There are intentionally no <include> or <exclude> rules, and that must stay
   that way:

   - Adding ANY <include> turns "back up everything" into "back up only these
     paths", silently dropping the Room database (servers, favourites, recorded
     certificates) and the DataStore settings from every backup.
   - Adding <exclude domain="file" path="user_certs"/> would silently disable
     the "Back up user certificate" setting: that setting works by MOVING the
     PKCS#12 files between filesDir/user_certs (included here) and
     noBackupFilesDir/user_certs, which the platform always excludes. See
     CertificateVault and UserCertificateStore.

   So the client certificate private key is kept out of backups by its location,
   not by a rule here: with the default setting off it lives in
   noBackupFilesDir, which neither Auto Backup nor device transfer ever reads.

   See https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/data/autobackup
-->
<full-backup-content>
</full-backup-content>
